{
  "id": "G17-screen-treats-silence-as-refusal",
  "gate": 17,
  "kind": "screen",
  "title": "Unanswered disclosure questions refuse rather than pass",
  "proves": "The blank template ships every question as null. If null read as 'no', a half-filled form would clear the regulated-data check while the operator believed they had skipped it. Silence is the most common way a disclosure fails to happen, so silence must refuse.",
